# Covers: the Lobby is in the chain of the realm a BATCH run uses, so a
#         bare `echo` resolves from a source file the same way it does
#         from a REPL line.  Spec section 6: "the CLI, batch mode, and
#         every REPL session get a realm whose chain includes the Lobby
#         proto".  Before the Lobby landed on root_globals this was a
#         lookup error, not output.
#
#         `echo(1)` also pins the coercion: echo renders a non-String
#         argument rather than raising, which is what makes `echo` usable
#         for the printf-debugging it exists for.
#
#         The line-mode half of the same claim is echo_in_line_mode.chk.
#         The two cannot be one fixture: -f prints no per-statement result
#         line and -i prints one, so their expected output differs by
#         exactly that line.
# matrix-row: lobby-echo

## mode: file

echo(1)
[00000000] *** 1
